# N2/P12 Results - Lazy Reuse Exactification and Derived Pair Statistics

## Status

P12 is complete. The frozen P8/P11 dispatch rule, `0.80` cutoff, P6 folding backend, Gate-P cases, natural EPFL cases, and timing protocol were unchanged. P12 changed only how the two remaining telemetry statistics are obtained.

Mandatory P11/P12 decision invariance passed on **332/332** frozen policy cases. Across those cases P12 performed only **34** reuse scans, with **11** terminating as soon as the frozen reuse threshold was provably exceeded. Fresh fuzz passed **1000/1000**.

P12 derives exact pair-repeat excess as `binary_nodes - distinct_pair_keys`, saturates per-pair counts at five, and computes reuse only if both the five-shell and pair-repeat predicates still leave annotation possible.

## Gate-P primary endpoint

| Comparison | Case-balanced geomean | 95% bootstrap CI | Workload-weighted | Wins |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| P12 / direct, source-inclusive | **1.019888x** | **0.950964-1.066939** | **0.982339x** | 3/36 |
| P12 / P11, source-inclusive | **0.978766x** | **0.969244-0.988333** | **0.979585x** | 28/36 |
| P12 / direct, source build | **1.281483x** | **1.255519-1.306823** | **1.292730x** | 0/36 |
| P12 / P11, source build | **0.934496x** | **0.921073-0.948385** | **0.933513x** | 34/36 |
| P12 / direct, selected compiler | **0.966997x** | **0.860367-1.045804** | **0.823343x** | 8/36 |

The preregistered **direct-crossover criterion failed**. P12's case-balanced point estimate is still **1.99% above direct**, and its confidence interval crosses 1. However, the workload-weighted full-pipeline result is **0.982339x direct**, i.e. about **1.77% below direct**. This is a secondary crossover, not the preregistered primary PASS.

P12 is nevertheless a clear improvement over P11: source-inclusive time is **0.978766x P11**, with the entire 95% interval below 1, and source construction is **0.934496x P11**. The predeclared lazy-statistics engineering criterion did **not** pass only because its deliberately stronger source-build target was `<=0.90`; the observed value was 0.934496x.

Median-of-case-median Gate-P source construction was approximately **48.0 us direct**, **67.1 us P11**, and **60.7 us P12**. Whole-pipeline medians were approximately **234.8 us**, **259.1 us**, and **254.5 us**.

## Lazy-statistics behavior

Only **6/36** Gate-P cases required any reuse scan. Five of those ultimately annotated; one terminated early after reuse exceeded the frozen threshold. Across all Gate-P cases, P12 scanned only **21.9%** as many reuse-classification edges as an eager all-case scan would have required.

No natural evaluation case required a reuse scan.

